@title Intent Restatement
@sigils [❄️/令]
@audience fulab agents, musn server
@tone technical
@style pattern
@why no problem-corpus source matched (@holds-at absent; holds-token and id-text searches over every node in [problems] found no match). Negative claim per the committed check futon2 holes labs library-loop runs l6_no_source_check.py, receipt runs/L10-no-source-check.edn. Rationale not invented (L10 rationale-backfill, zai-1, 2026-09-05)
@how own mechanism: Start the response with a one-line intent restatement. (source: this pattern's ! conclusion line; L10 rationale-backfill, zai-1, 2026-09-05)

! conclusion: Start the response with a one-line intent restatement.

  + context: The agent must align its response to the user task and patterns.

  + IF:
    The response begins without an explicit intent line.

  + HOWEVER:
    The run still needs momentum; we should avoid long preambles.

  + THEN:
    Begin with "Intent: <one-line restatement>" before plans or tools.

  + BECAUSE:
    A crisp intent line improves PSR/PUR anchoring and human review.

  + NEXT-STEPS:
    - evidence: first assistant line starts with "Intent:".
    - evidence-shape: {:intent :string}
